  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.0 contains two breaking changes: Nip.IssuingTaxOfficePrefix now returns string (zero-padded, e.g. \"012\") instead of int, and the out parameter names on TryParse overloads for Pesel, Nip, and Regon were renamed from identifier-specific names to result. It also adds TypeConverter support for Pesel, Nip, and Regon, TryParse(string?, IFormatProvider?, out T) overloads for ASP.NET Core Minimal API binding on all supported targets, and NipGenerator.Invalid.UnrecognizedFormat(). See CHANGELOG.md for details.",
